WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
The data booklet lists a standard
enthalpy of formation for methane.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.490
That's the enthalpy change when one mole
of methane forms from carbon and hydrogen.

3
00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.170
But carbon and hydrogen don't
combine cleanly to make methane,

4
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:15.310
so no one can simply measure it.

5
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.170
So how does the data
booklet know its value?

6
00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:22.030
In this mission, you'll pin down
standard conditions and standard states,

7
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.690
and define enthalpies of
formation and combustion.

8
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:28.370
You'll use formation data
in Hess's law cycles,

9
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:31.650
starting with the
decomposition of limestone.

10
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:32.670
Your mission:

11
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:37.410
work out how a value no one can measure
directly gets into the data booklet.
